rue\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Marinade Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Soy Sauce</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Sesame Oil</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Honey</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Rice Vinegar</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">3</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cloves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Garlic (minced)</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">inch</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Ginger (grated)</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Chili Flakes</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Green Onions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Green Onions (sliced)</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-3132-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3132\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing marinade</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Resealable Bag or Container&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For marinating chicken</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-3132-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-3132-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3132\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation Steps</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3132-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In a bowl, whisk together 1/2 cup of soy sauce, 2 tablespoons of sesame oil, 2 tablespoons of honey, and 1 tablespoon of rice vinegar. Add 3 minced garlic cloves, 1 inch of grated ginger, and a pinch of chili flakes for a little kick. Mix until well combined.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3132-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Chop 2-3 green onions and stir them into the marinade. This adds a fresh flavor and a pop of color!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3132-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Place your chicken pieces in a resealable bag or container. Pour the marinade over the chicken, making sure it’s well coated. Seal the bag or container and refrigerate for at least 2 hours, or overnight for maximum flavor.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3132-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">When you’re ready to cook, remove the chicken from the marinade and shake off any excess. Grill, bake, or pan-sear the chicken until it’s fully cooked, about 20-30 minutes depending on your method. Enjoy your deliciously marinated chicken!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-3132-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>200</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>8g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>20g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>10g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here&#8217;s how to prepare your tasty Asian chicken marinade!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Asian-Chicken-Marinade.webp\" alt=\"A kitchen table displaying various ingredients for an asian chicken marinade, including soy sauce, sesame oil, honey, rice vinegar, garlic, ginger, chili flakes, and green onions.\" class=\"wp-image-3130\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Asian-Chicken-Marinade.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Asian-Chicken-Marinade-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Soy Sauce</strong> – 1/2 cup</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Sesame Oil</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Honey</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Rice Vinegar</strong> – 1 tablespoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Garlic (minced)</strong> – 3 cloves</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Ginger (grated)</strong> – 1 inch</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Chili Flakes</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Green Onions (sliced)</strong> – 2</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-asian-chicken-marinade\"><strong>How to Make Asian Chicken Marinade</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to elevate your chicken game with this delightful Asian chicken marinade! With just a bit of prep, you’ll have juicy, flavorful chicken that’s perfect for grilling, baking, or pan-searing. The total preparation time is about 10 minutes, and you’ll want to let it <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marination\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">marinate </a>for at least 2 hours, or even overnight for the best flavor. Cooking time will vary depending on your method, but it typically takes around 20-30 minutes. Let’s dive in!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/How-to-Make-Asian-Chicken-Marinade.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making asian chicken marinade, including whisking ingredients, adding green onions, marinating chicken, and cooking.\" class=\"wp-image-3131\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/How-to-Make-Asian-Chicken-Marinade.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/How-to-Make-Asian-Chicken-Marinade-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Whisk Together Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a bowl, whisk together 1/2 cup of soy sauce, 2 tablespoons of sesame oil, 2 tablespoons of honey, and 2 tablespoons of rice vinegar. Add 3 minced garlic cloves, 1 tablespoon of grated ginger, and a pinch of chili flakes for a little kick. Mix until well combined.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Add Green Onions</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Chop 2-3 green onions and stir them into the marinade. This adds a fresh flavor and a pop of color!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Marinate the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place your chicken pieces in a resealable bag or container. Pour the marinade over the chicken, making sure it’s well coated. Seal the bag or container and refrigerate for at least 2 hours, or overnight for maximum flavor.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Cook the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When you’re ready to cook, remove the chicken from the marinade and shake off any excess. Grill, bake, or pan-sear the chicken until it’s fully cooked, about 20-30 minutes depending on your method. Enjoy your deliciously marinated chicken!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Asian</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>30 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>120 minutes (Marinating)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>160 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>High Protein</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Grilled or baked with fresh sides!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-asian-chicken-marinade\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Asian Chicken Marinade</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Marinate for at least 30 minutes for deeper flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use fresh ginger and garlic for a vibrant taste.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Balance sweetness with a splash of lime juice.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Try adding sesame oil for a nutty aroma.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Always taste and adjust seasoning before cooking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-asian-chicken-marinade\"><strong>How to Serve this asian chicken marinade</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve over a bed of fluffy jasmine rice for a comforting meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with steamed broccoli or bok choy for a fresh crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap in lettuce leaves for a fun, low-carb option.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top a salad with sliced grilled chicken for a zesty lunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use in a stir-fry with colorful veggies for a quick dinner.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a side of coconut rice for a tropical twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Make delicious chicken tacos with Asian slaw for a fusion treat.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and preparing your Asian chicken marinade ahead of time is simple and convenient:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Transfer leftovers to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date for easy tracking.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Pour marinade into a freezer-safe bag or container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Remove excess air to prevent freezer burn.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 3 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight before reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat in a saucepan over medium heat until warmed through.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stir occasionally for even heating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve immediately for the best flavor and texture.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What to marinate chicken in Asian?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To create a delicious Asian chicken marinade, you can use a combination of soy sauce, ginger, garlic, sesame oil, and a touch of honey or brown sugar for sweetness. This blend not only infuses the chicken with rich flavors but also helps to tenderize the meat, making it juicy and flavorful after cooking.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. How do Asian restaurants get their chicken so tender?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Asian restaurants often use techniques like marinating the chicken in a mixture that includes soy sauce, cornstarch, and sometimes baking soda. The cornstarch creates a protective coating that locks in moisture, while baking soda helps to break down proteins, resulting in incredibly tender chicken. Additionally, they may use quick cooking methods like stir-frying to keep the chicken juicy.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What do Chinese restaurants marinate their chicken in?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Chinese restaurants typically marinate chicken in a mixture of soy sauce, oyster sauce, ginger, garlic, and sometimes a bit of sugar or honey. This combination not only adds depth of flavor but also helps to tenderize the chicken, ensuring it remains moist and flavorful when cooked. Some may also include rice vinegar for a hint of acidity.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. What do Asians put on chicken to make it tender?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To make chicken tender, many <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asian_cuisine\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Asian cuisines</a> use marinades that include ingredients like soy sauce, ginger, and a bit of sugar. Additionally, some recipes incorporate a small amount of baking soda, which helps to break down the proteins in the chicken, resulting in a more tender texture. Marinating for a few hours or overnight can significantly enhance the tenderness and flavor of the chicken.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that you have the best Asian chicken marinade recipe, it’s time to unleash your inner chef! Picture the aroma filling your kitchen as you grill or bake your chicken to perfection. It’s simple, rewarding, and oh-so-delicious! So gather your ingredients, invite some friends over, and enjoy a meal that’s sure to create lasting memories. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
